Guided Exercise: Update Application Image and Settings
Objectives
•	Pause, update, and resume deployments.
•	Roll back a failing deployment.
•	Minimize service interruption for database and web applications.
________________________________________
Part 1: Updating the Database Deployment
1. Log in and select project
oc login -u developer -p developer https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
oc project updates-rollout-db
2. Inspect current deployment
oc get deployment -o wide
oc get pod
oc get pod <pod-name> -o jsonpath='{.spec.containers[0].image}{"\n"}'
•	Database uses rhel9/mysql-80:1-224.
3. Connect to database
oc rsh <pod-name> mysql --user=operator1 --password=test -e "SHOW DATABASES"
•	Confirm you can access quotes database.
4. Pause deployment
oc rollout pause deployment/mydb
5. Update environment variable (password)
oc set env deployment/mydb MYSQL_PASSWORD=redhat123
•	Confirm password not yet active (deployment paused).
6. Update container image
oc set image deployment/mydb mysql-80=registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/rhel9/mysql-80:1-228
•	Verify old pod still uses 1-224.
7. Resume deployment
oc rollout resume deployment/mydb
oc get pods
oc get pod <new-pod-name> -o jsonpath='{.spec.containers[0].image}{"\n"}'
•	Confirm new pod uses 1-228 image.
•	Verify new password works:
oc rsh <new-pod-name> mysql --user=operator1 --password=redhat123 -e "SHOW DATABASES"
________________________________________
Part 2: Rolling Update of Web Application
1. Switch project
oc project updates-rollout-web
2. Inspect deployment and ReplicaSet
oc get deployment -o wide
oc get replicaset
oc get replicaset <replicaset-name> -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].image}{"\n"}'
•	Current image: redhattraining/versioned-hello:v1.0.
•	Confirm readiness probe exists (HTTP GET on port 8080).
3. Start continuous requests to monitor updates
/home/student/DO180/labs/updates-rollout/curl_loop.sh
4. Update deployment image
oc set image deployment/version versioned-hello=registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/versioned-hello:v1.1
•	Rolling update occurs:
o	Old pods (v1.0) and new pods (v1.1) respond simultaneously.
o	After rollout, only v1.1 responds.
5. Confirm rollout
oc rollout status deployment/version
oc get replicaset
oc get replicaset <new-replicaset-name> -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].image}{"\n"}'
6. Rollback deployment
oc rollout undo deployment/version
•	Old pods (v1.0) scale up; new pods (v1.1) scale down.
•	Confirm by checking ReplicaSets and curl_loop.sh.
________________________________________
Key Takeaways
1.	Pausing deployments allows multiple changes before rollout.
2.	RollingUpdate strategy minimizes downtime for replicated services.
3.	Recreate strategy is used when simultaneous versions cannot run.
4.	Readiness probes ensure traffic goes to ready pods.
5.	Rollbacks are managed via ReplicaSets (oc rollout undo).
6.	Environment variables and images can be updated separately and safely.

